Second View Point
 BUSINESS VIEW POINT
The first phone call made by a mobile phone was on the 3rd of April 1973. It was made by an engineer named Marty Cooper who worked at the telecommunications firm in Motorola, the call was made to a rival at his company's competitor named Bell Laboratories. Then mobile phone was first introduced in the year 1984, and it was called the Motorola Dynatac 8000X. At the time it was sold for $3995, that’s approximately $11,700 or £9,500 today. At the time, the average weekly wage in the UK was around £117 and for that time people could only call people with the mobile phones and that was it. 
In the beginning mobile phones were only being used by business people who were busy at the time and needed to get in touch with clients and colleagues throughout the da and mostly because they were the ones who could afford it.

From a business view piont the evolution from mobile phones to smart phones helped make communication from companies end users significantly easier and faster. traditional mobile phones were mostly used for just texting and calling but whene smart phones were introduced they helped provide access to the internent, online shopping, advertising, social media and other business applications. 
